  "changelog": {
    "version": "0.3.0",
    "title": "River Client 0.3.0",
    "summary": "A cleaner River menu, a Keybinds page, performance mods by default, 26.3 launching again, and the lyrics crash fixed.",
    "items": [
      "New: The River menu uses a smooth font and quieter cards. The Minecraft styles keep the pixel font.",
      "New: Clicking a module in the HUD editor opens its settings beside it, so changes show in place.",
      "New: Every River instance gets Sodium, Lithium, FerriteCore, ImmediatelyFast, Entity Culling and more once, on its next launch. Remove any of them and they stay removed. Skipped with OptiFine.",
      "New: Usage stats switch in launcher Settings.",
      "New: Keybinds page in the River menu. Every River key in one list, and the menu key can be changed.",
      "New: Custom Text module. Your own lines with live values like {fps} and {ping}.",
      "New: Teleport to a waypoint, when the server lets you use /tp.",
      "New: Realms button on River's main menu.",
      "New: HUD modules pushed against each other join into one panel.",
      "Improved: Start typing anywhere in the River menu to search, and it opens where you left it.",
      "Improved: River costs less FPS. Glass blur and Coordinates were the most expensive parts.",
      "Improved: River no longer reads your login token itself, and the launcher no longer has old certificate code, so fewer scanners flag it.",
      "Fixed: 26.3 instances not starting with \"1 confirmed mod compatibility issue\".",
      "Fixed: The game crashing on 26.3 when lyrics or waypoint names showed new letters.",
      "Fixed: Time Changer, module icons on the title screen, the cape in the main menu preview, GUI scale after leaving full screen, and River's HUD showing in Flashback replays.",
      "Fixed: Cancelling a launch before the game starts.",
      "Improved: Launcher updates are signed, so an altered update list is ignored."
    ]
  },
  "notes": "A cleaner River menu, a Keybinds page, performance mods by default, 26.3 launching again, and the lyrics crash fixed.",
